{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793210868,"nonce":"m67Su5hcTk+ZgeHKEDa0U5QceS8=","title":"Convert macro position character offsets to internal UTF-8 spans","message":"A real Ashui nested button has a class hover without preceding Unicode text, but falls back to the whole Markup.build expansion after a preceding ellipsis. Pocket Studio BoardHeader contains a Unicode ellipsis in its input placeholder before its buttons; For tag positions were a separate after-tag-name mapping gap.\n\nStock Haxe 4.3.6 evidence: a macro argument whose markup begins at character 51 and ends at character 81 has Context.getPosInfos min=51,max=81, even though its UTF-8 byte range ends at 83. Macro string a…b has length 3 and indexOf(b)=2. Rayzor's macro string indexes agree, but Context.getPosInfos and makePosition previously exposed/accepted raw UTF-8 byte offsets. Combining their byte offsets with parser character indexes shifts subsequent constructors and diagnostics.\n\nConvert offsets at the Context API boundary, retaining byte offsets internally for the parser and editor. Register the actual source before macro execution, including editor overrides, so conversion does not use stale on-disk text. Cover named-position round trips, virtual source contents, non-BMP characters, and constructor hover after an unsaved edit that changes the prefix length.\n\nReproducers: /tmp/rayzor-ashui-direct-button-position (installed Ashui 0.2.0) and /tmp/rayzor-stock-macro-string-position. Before logs: /tmp/rayzor-ashui-direct-button-position-unicode-before.log and /tmp/rayzor-stock-macro-string-position.log. Portable regression: unicode_macro_positions_follow_the_current_document.","files":null}]}